WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.870
Nobody has time.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.510
Or so we say.

3
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.280
I hear it differently.

4
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.430
When someone tells me
they don't have time,

5
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.610
I hear something else:

6
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.930
I don't know how to manage my time.

7
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.260
I don't know how to delegate.

8
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.630
I don't know how to build a structure.

9
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.970
My own lesson came from swimming.

10
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.660
I swam for years, hours a day,

11
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.670
before school and after.

12
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.550
To get good at one thing, you pick one.

13
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.510
You can't be good at
three or four at once.

14
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.060
And once you finish one thing,

15
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.880
you learn how you got there:

16
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:39.200
the discipline, the goals, the process.

17
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.310
Even if you leave that field,

18
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.110
you keep the roadmap.

19
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.770
So here's the question.

20
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.280
What did you start and leave unfinished?

21
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.080
What would finishing it have taught you?

